    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, and the one existing test passes.\n\nIt makes one `client.messages.create` call to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5`. The system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from `bug, feature, question`, and the ticket text is sent as the user message. It joins the text blocks of the reply, strips and lower-cases the result, and returns `\"question\"` if that isn't one of `LABELS`.\n\n**Temperature:** the pinned SDK (`anthropic==1.8.0`) no longer has a `temperature` argument on `messages.create`, so passing `temperature=0` directly would raise a `TypeError`. The SDK's migration guide says to send it through `extra_body` for older models like `claude-sonnet-4-6` that still accept it, so the call uses `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`. One thing to know: newer models such as Sonnet 5 and the Opus 4.7+/5 line reject `temperature` with a 400 error. If `MODEL` is ever changed to one of those, this call will fail and you'll have to give up temperature 0 on that model.\n\n**Check:** I ran the function against a fake HTTP transport, so no real API call was made. The request body contained `model`, `max_tokens: 5`, `system`, the user message and `temperature: 0`. A reply of `\" Bug\\n\"` came back as `bug`.\n\nI couldn't delete the temporary check script `_check.py` in the project root because the `rm` needed approval. You can delete it."
